/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/21897d95/25/code.py:40:#      deliberate vertical->horizontal interaction chain that changes the phase-2 source.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:18:#   variant. The fusion keeps the original "plug notch -> follow cavity chain" rule,
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:19:#   then applies panel packing, but now there are 3-4 chains and each chain is short
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:25:#   sprites. Output is the same 30x30 scene after assembling 1-2 longer chains.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:27:#   solve the full scene first, then crop each solved chain together with its bar strip
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:30:#   instead of 1-2 deeper chains of length 2-3, build 3-4 shallower chains of length
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:35:#   2. Track each chain separately.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:36:#   3. Pack each chain into its own panel together with only its matching bar strip.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:40:#   - combo: pieces A/B, C, D/E, F become four separate solved chains; return four
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:41:#     left-to-right panels, each panel containing one chain and the corresponding bar
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:45:# - If the generator allowed only 1-2 chains, the fusion would collapse visually back
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:46:#   toward the original task or plain D7. I therefore force 3-4 chains.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:47:# - If every chain had length 1, the cavity-following rule would become too weak. I
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:48:#   therefore force at least one 2-piece chain in every sample, while keeping the total
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:56:#   boundary and chains still grow perpendicular to that side.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:58:#   broken by 3-4 chain samples, so the fusion raises the root subset limit to 4 and
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:59:#   prefers solutions with more chains.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:61:#   now always reconstructs the full scene internally and only then repacks the chains.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:63:#   each intended chain owns a unique strip interval `[A, B]` and panels should be
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:70:# - Used strips are chosen with explicit gaps, used notches never overlap, chain pieces
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:78:#      chains rather than long cascades.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:83:# - Each panel is a tight crop of one chain plus its bar strip, so unrelated decoy holes
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:90:# - The only new global inference is layout: "solve each local chain, then display each
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:91:#   solved chain as a separate panel".
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:94:# - `main()` now prefers more-chain explanations before fewer-chain explanations. The
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:95:#   generator must therefore never create two intended chains that share a strip interval
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:96:#   or reuse the same root piece shape in a way that makes a lower-chain interpretation
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:98:# - Some generated chains are length-1 rectangles. That is a new allowance compared with
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/11/code.py:100:#   "short-chain breadth" visually obvious.
